 ## Key Design Decisions
 
 - **Commands over HTTPS, one authoritative board per event.** Editors submit commands to the server, which assigns each committed edit one event revision. Peer-to-peer or browser-side merging was rejected: the tenets require one authoritative revision regardless of delivery route, and offline editing is a non-goal.
+- **Self-hosted WebSockets for change delivery.** Committed changes are pushed to browsers over self-hosted WebSocket connections, accepting connection capacity and reconnect operations in exchange for fast updates without recurring realtime vendor fees or provider coupling. Five-second HTTPS polling (simpler stateless operation, but repeated reads and several seconds of lag) and a hosted realtime service (less connection ops, but recurring fees and provider coupling) were rejected. See [Change Delivery Mechanism](decisions/change-delivery.md).
